<title>PORTUGAL: Yield rises on Portuguese 182-day bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Portuguese 182-day bills.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield rose to 5.7276 percent, from 5.6058 percent previously, at the Institute for Public Credit Management's (IGCP) sale of 182-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The IGCP placed 30 billion escudos.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
